    "turn_text": "is to uh... so we we want to provide uh... members uh... with input uh... into what it does uh... or the new office of the new congressional office of technology uh... by having making sure we have a member day every legislative session where members can come and testify before the OTA governing board to explore certain issues or to come and make suggestions about what OTA should be doing. We also provide members with expertise with quicker turnaround times. We want to emphasize that information that members request should be provided as quickly as possible. One of the frustrations with the general accountable of the office or GAO studies is, one, you have to get them approved, which is cumbersome and two, they often take a long time to get those done. We also like the idea of of emulating some of the work that the Congressional Research Service does in terms of their style. In other words, they would deliver briefings and informal conversations and technical assistance to members without the need for the oversight board to approve everything. So, you know, as well as objective policy options when requested. So, you know, you have to go with this, find a person from the other party to write a joint letter to the powers that be a GAO to get a service. We want this to be a very user-friendly service for members. And this is the one I really like is to say GAO, say the Office of Technology Assessment is doing a more robust analysis of a certain topic in technology. We like the idea of members getting preliminary findings of the",
