    "turn_idx": 15,
    "turn_text": "I think members are... I just came out of a classified briefing about technology today. You know, members that are, I would say relatively young, carrying around their cell phones, are trying to understand the ways in which security can be compromised in those cell phones. And there's a few people who have Very few of us are trained in counter-intelligence and just how electronics, one of my staffers was saying, oh, my roommate who is not a congressional employee is going to China. And she advised her roommate, you ought to. You got to get like a throwaway phone or a burner phone or a temporary phone that you take with you to China. And the reaction was, oh, she just laughed in my face kind of thing. So I'm paranoid. And members of Congress say, that's a very real stress that members feel, especially in light of what happened in the 2016 election year. The technology and the anxiety around technology and the anxiety about not understanding its limitations, its perils, is something that's going to, I think, be increasingly in members' faces. And it's going to take maybe one or two more",
